<div class="sop-meta">
  <div><strong>Trigger</strong> Inbound contact form, email, phone/text, referral, or LinkedIn message</div>
  <div><strong>Owner</strong> Whoever sees it first; same-day response is the SLA</div>
  <div><strong>Time</strong> 5-15 min triage + initial reply</div>
  <div><strong>Output</strong> Reply sent &amp; lead logged in CRM</div>
</div>

<h2>Channels</h2>
<p>Five inbound channels. All five reach the same primary email address; I do not split them across multiple inboxes.</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Contact form</strong> at <code>/contact/</code> &middot; ~70% of leads. Submission goes to Web3Forms which forwards to the primary inbox.</li>
  <li><strong>Direct email</strong> to the published business address &middot; ~15%. Often referrals or returning visitors.</li>
  <li><strong>Phone or text</strong> to the published number &middot; ~10%. Voicemail rolls to a transcription.</li>
  <li><strong>Referrals</strong> from existing clients (and the <code>/refer/</code> form) &middot; ~5%. Highest close rate.</li>
  <li><strong>LinkedIn / community DMs</strong> &middot; ~&lt;5%. Treat as email.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Triage decision tree</h2>
<p>Within 5 minutes of seeing the lead, decide one of four paths.</p>

<h3>A. Strong fit, schedule discovery call</h3>
<p>Lead is a US/Canada-based small service business, owner-led, has an existing site they want replaced or no site at all, indicates flat-rate pricing is acceptable. Reply within 4 business hours with a discovery-call link.</p>

<h3>B. Strong fit but not yet ready</h3>
<p>"Maybe in 6 months" / "Just exploring" responses. Reply with a brief educational note, link to <a href="/what-we-build/">/what-we-build/</a>, and add to a follow-up reminder for 90 days out.</p>

<h3>C. Out of scope, refer out</h3>
<p>E-commerce store with 100+ SKUs, app-shaped problem (booking system with inventory, dashboards), or industry I do not serve well (large enterprise, government, regulated medical). Reply with a polite decline + a recommendation if we know one.</p>

<h3>D. Spam / low-signal</h3>
<p>SEO outreach, link-building pitches, "I will boost your rankings" emails, AI-generated cold outbound. Mark as spam in inbox; no reply.</p>

<h2>Steps</h2>
<ul class="sop-checklist">
  <li>Open the inbound. Read it once fully before classifying.</li>
  <li>Check the URL the lead shares (if any) for: existing site stack, current PageSpeed score, location, business size.</li>
  <li>Open <a href="https://www.google.com/maps">Google Maps</a> for their address. Verify the business is real and the GBP is set up.</li>
  <li>Decide A/B/C/D from the tree above.</li>
  <li>Send the matching reply (templates below). Include their name and at least one specific reference to their email so it doesn't read as canned.</li>
  <li>Log in CRM: name, email, channel, decision, date.</li>
  <li>If A: schedule the discovery call. If B: set the 90-day follow-up reminder. If C: send the referral if applicable.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Reply templates</h2>

<div class="sop-template">
  <div class="sop-template-label">Template A &middot; schedule discovery call</div>
<pre>Hi {first_name},

Thanks for reaching out, {specific_reference_to_their_email}.

Sounds like a good fit for what we do. Want to grab 20 minutes to talk
through what you're looking for and what we'd build? No pitch deck, no
pressure. The first call is just us asking what you've got and what you
want.

Pick a slot here: {calendar_link}

Or reply with a few times that work and I'll confirm.

— Jon
Pikes Peak Web Designs
{phone}</pre>
</div>

<div class="sop-template">
  <div class="sop-template-label">Template B &middot; not yet ready</div>
<pre>Hi {first_name},

Appreciate you reaching out. Sounds like a good potential fit; just not
the right moment to start a build.

I'll bookmark this and circle back in {timeframe}. If you want to move
faster, our /what-we-build/ page has the full deliverable laid out:
https://pikespeakwebdesigns.com/what-we-build/

In the meantime, no pressure. Reach out any time you want to talk.

— Jon</pre>
</div>

<div class="sop-template">
  <div class="sop-template-label">Template C &middot; out of scope, refer out</div>
<pre>Hi {first_name},

Thanks for the note. Honest answer: this isn't our specialty. We focus on
small US/Canadian service businesses on flat-rate marketing sites; what
you're describing is {their_actual_need}, which is a different shape of
build.

{recommended_specialist} does this well; their site is {url}. I have no
financial relationship with them, just sending you toward someone who
can do right by you.

Best of luck with the project.

— Jon</pre>
</div>

<h2>Common issues</h2>

<div class="sop-callout">
  <strong>The lead is vague ("just curious about pricing")</strong>
  Don't auto-decline. Reply with a one-liner asking what they currently have for a website. Often the follow-up reveals strong fit.
</div>

<div class="sop-callout">
  <strong>The lead is a referral from an existing client</strong>
  Always reply within 1 hour during business hours, even if it's just "got it, replying in detail tonight." Referrals close 3x; speed matters.
</div>

<div class="sop-callout sop-callout--warn">
  <strong>The lead pushes for an immediate quote without a call</strong>
  Polite firm: "happy to quote, but the 20-min call lets us scope it correctly. The form alone never gives us enough to commit a price." Don't quote sight-unseen.
</div>

<div class="sop-callout sop-callout--warn">
  <strong>Cold outbound from an "agency" offering to buy our domain</strong>
  Spam. Ignore.
</div>

<h2>Exit criteria</h2>
<p>Lead is logged + replied to + classified within 4 business hours. If A, the discovery call is on the calendar. We move to <a href="/sop/discovery-call/">phase 02</a> when the call happens.</p>
